			<div class="content" id="post-content-4823568">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX can relay information from &quot;Daddy&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>how does it relay information and why would you call it daddy</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Empirical evidence of -1's were discovered after findings of black slanted metamorphic spikes underneath the earth after excavation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It's not actually clear what -1 is here; SCP-XXXX is the general rock, SCP-XXXX-2 is uh 'the father' but -1 is just kinda&#8230;there?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX goes into a tantrum after being ignored for a prolonged amount of time. This results in a natural disaster 16 to 24 hours because of anger from -1 and -2.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I generally would urge you to avoid adding properties like this where it's like 'you have to interact with the SCP or bad things': having a reason for people to interact with it generally ends up with you creating a much more interesting narrative; whereas if they have to, it always makes the outcome of it feel&#8230;cheap</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX has a voice of a male baby</p>
</blockquote>
<p>why?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>His drunkenness also led him to come back to the facility one day and think that SCP-XXXX was the child he had with his women.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I do not like your new narrative and I think this line is perhaps the one I can best highlight to explain why: it's dumb, it feels irrelevant to the whole thing about like, the giant rock under the earth and the weather prediction and it doesn't really make any sense for a person to do.</p>
<p>I like the idea of using the Agent as a like, proxy for the father and having this kinda revolve around 'daddy' issues as a result but the actual execution feels extremely on the nose and just&#8230;ridiculous.</p>
<p>The juxtaposition of this rock being like&#8230;a baby and also calling for what is effectively the eradication of a country by natural disaster feels&#8230;jarring in an unpleasant way, in particular because the idea of this rock being a baby just feels&#8230;not good and also unclear as to why it's the case?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

